"Friday",KG1="Saturday",JG1="Sunday",XG1="January",QG1="February",YG1="March",eK1="April",aK1="May",tK1="June",nK1="July",lK1="August",rK1="September",cK1="October",oK1="November",mK1="December",iK1="Latest Articles",sK1="read",hK1="Read more",AK1="Work | Digitaltableteur",ZK1="Selected projects and experiments by Digitaltableteur",dK1="Blog | Digitaltableteur",uK1="Insights and articles from the Digitaltableteur team",HK1="Cookie Policy | Digitaltableteur",pK1="How Digitaltableteur uses cookies and your choices about them",VK1="Designing in 2025 | Digitaltableteur",MK1="Navigating the AI-assisted creative landscape.",EK1="Digitaltableteur Field Notes: In Search of Impact | Digitaltableteur",gK1="How a solo studio delivers enterprise-scale outcomes with boutique precision.",fK1="Workflow Tips | Digitaltableteur",LK1="A behind-the-scenes look at how we keep projects moving.",vK1="Digital Craftsmanship | Digitaltableteur",wK1="Thoughts on maintaining quality in a hurry-up culture.",yK1="Figma MCP, Design Systems, and Generative UI | Digitaltableteur",FK1="How Figma's MCP server speeds up design-to-code workflows.",$K1="Thoughts on Future Branding | Digitaltableteur",CK1="Exploring branding in the age of AI and exponential design.",IK1="Petri Lahdelma: A Biography | Digitaltableteur",bK1="From Varissuo to leading global design systems.",SK1="Digitaltableteur logo",kK1="An error image indicating a missing or inaccessible resource.",RK1="Go back to Home",NK1="Cookie consent",TK1='Digitaltableteur uses cookies to improve your experience. Choosing "Accept all" enables optional analytics cookies. Selecting "Only essential" stores only the cookies required for the site to function.',xK1="Read our",PK1="cookie policy",DK1="to learn more.",_K1="AI use & transparency",BK1="Accept all",OK1="Only essential",jK1="Cookie policy",zK1="We use cookies to remember your preferences and to analyze how our site is used. Essential cookies are saved automatically because the site cannot operate without them.",UK1='Analytics cookies are enabled only if you click "Accept all" on the modal. Choosing "Only essential" keeps these disabled. You can change your preference at any time through your browser settings.',WK1="For details about how we handle personal data and your rights under GDPR, please contact us.",qK1="To comply with EU law, we clearly separate cookies by purpose, keep a log of the choices made, and refresh consent at least every 13 months.",GK1="Cookie categories we use",KK1="Essential – required for login-free navigation, consent storage, and website security. These are first-party cookies with short lifetimes.",JK1="Analytics – collect aggregated usage data via privacy-friendly tooling. They are stored only when you opt in.",XK1="Functional – remember language, theme, or embed settings to keep the experience consistent.",QK1="Marketing/community – enable previews from services like Substack or Instagram. Disabled unless you consent.",YK1="Managing your consent",eJ1='Use the banner to revise your choice. You can also reopen it by clearing the "cookieConsent" entry in your browser’s storage or contacting mail@digitaltableteur.com so we can reset your preference.',aJ1="Parts of the site are created or tested with AI-assisted tooling. Details about those workflows are listed in our",tJ1="AI use transparency statement",nJ1="AI use and transparency",lJ1="Read how Digitaltableteur uses AI-assisted tools, the safeguards we apply, and your rights under EU law.",rJ1="AI use & transparency statement",cJ1="We apply AI-assisted services carefully and in line with the EU AI Act and GDPR. Humans stay responsible for every deliverable, and we track each tool that touches client or visitor data.",oJ1="Where AI is used",mJ1="Design exploration – generating alternative layouts or colour palettes for internal review. AI suggestions are always reviewed by a senior designer before implementation.",iJ1="Editorial assistance – drafting article outlines, alt texts, or translations that are later fact-checked and edited by a human.",sJ1="Quality assurance – analysing anonymised support tickets and telemetry to improve accessibility and performance.",hJ1="Data we send to AI providers",AJ1="We only share the prompts necessary for the task at hand, remove personal identifiers whenever possible, and opt out of provider-side training. Sensitive production data is never sent to public models.",ZJ1="Governance & safeguards",dJ1="Human review – every AI output is validated by an accountable team member before being published or delivered to a client.",uJ1="Data minimisation – prompts are truncated, masked, or sampled so that individuals cannot be identified.",HJ1="Vendor review – we only use providers that offer EU-grade security and data processing agreements.",pJ1="Your rights",VJ1="Right to information – you can ask us which AI systems touched your project or data at any time.",MJ1="Right to object – you may request that we avoid AI-assisted tooling in your assignment. We will confirm feasibility and document the alternative workflow.",EJ1="Right to erasure – if AI tooling touched personal data, you can request deletion or expect it to follow the retention limits in our contract.",gJ1="To exercise these rights, email mail@digitaltableteur.com or contact us via the channels listed in the privacy policy.",fJ1="Template Article Title | Digitaltableteur",LJ1="Template description for future articles.",vJ1="Share",wJ1="Site Under Development! 🚧 Stay tuned!",yJ1="Work",FJ1="Prev",$J1="Next",CJ1="New Things Co",IJ1="Illustrations",bJ1="Primary",SJ1="Secondary",kJ1="Tertiary",RJ1="Error",NJ1="Warning",TJ1="Success",xJ1="Info",PJ1="Left Icon",DJ1="Right Icon",_J1="Disabled",BJ1="Small",OJ1="Medium",jJ1="Large",zJ1="Remove badge",UJ1="Primary",WJ1="Secondary",qJ1="Success",GJ1="Info",KJ1="Error",JJ1="Warning",XJ1="Neutral",QJ1="Removable Badge",YJ1="Small",eX1="Medium",aX1="Large",tX1="Quality Dashboard",nX1="Realtime snapshot of automated testing, accessibility coverage, and Storybook health.",lX1="Last updated {{date}}",rX1="Vitest Summary",cX1="Latest unit and integration suite results across the application.",oX1="Page Accessibility",mX1="Automated axe-core sweep of high-traffic routes.",iX1="Storybook Accessibility",sX1="Accessibility checks for published Storybook stories.",hX1="Vitest Coverage",AX1="Track how coverage compares against the enforced CI gate.",ZX1="{{passed}} / {{total}} metrics on target",dX1="Statements",uX1="Branches",HX1="Functions",pX1="Lines",VX1="On target",MX1="Needs attention",EX1="Target {{target}}",gX1="Design System Adoption",fX1="Percentage of shipped views using the latest component library.",LX1="{{rate}} adoption",vX1="Target {{target}}",wX1="Design to Implementation",yX1="Average lead time to ship designs as production-ready components.",FX1="Average {{days}} days",$X1="95th percentile {{days}} days",CX1="Target {{days}} days",IX1="Data freshness",bX1="Metrics snapshot generated {{date}}. Run the CI pipeline to refresh this data.",SX1="unknown",kX1="Total tests",RX1="Passed",NX1="Failed",TX1="Tests",xX1="Test suites",PX1="Page routes",DX1="Stories",_X1="Visual Regression",BX1="Automated image diff results from Storybook visual regression tests.",OX1="{{count}} visual change(s)",jX1="{{count}} visual change",zX1="{{count}} visual changes",UX1="Last visual run {{date}}",WX1="Baseline",qX1="Current build",GX1="Diff overlay",KX1="Visual tests are running",JX1="The latest Storybook visual regression results will appear here once available.",XX1="No visual changes detected",QX1="All Storybook stories match the stored baselines. Visual diffs will appear automatically when changes are detected.",YX1="Could not load visual diff report",eQ1="Baseline screenshot for {{story}}",aQ1="Current screenshot for {{story}}",tQ1="Diff overlay for {{story}}",nQ1="Digitaltableteur Storybook",lQ1="Your hub for component previews, documentation, and quality dashboards.",rQ1="Quick Links",c